# React Component Standards

## Component Structure

Always use functional components with this file order:

1. Imports (React, libraries, local)
2. Types/interfaces (export if shared)
3. Component function (named export)

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — default export, inline types
export default function Card({ title, desc }: { title: string; desc: string }) {
  return <div>{title}</div>;
}

// ✅ GOOD — named export, typed props interface
interface ClientCardProps {
  clientName: string;
  panNumber: string;
  servicesCount: number;
  onClick: () => void;
}

export function ClientCard({ clientName, panNumber, servicesCount, onClick }: ClientCardProps) {
  return (
    <button onClick={onClick} className="rounded-lg border p-4 text-left hover:bg-muted">
      <h3 className="font-semibold">{clientName}</h3>
      <p className="text-sm text-muted-foreground">PAN: {panNumber}</p>
      <p className="text-sm">{servicesCount} active services</p>
    </button>
  );
}
```

## Rules

- Always use **named exports**, never default exports
- Props interface named `{ComponentName}Props`, defined above the component
- Destructure props in function signature
- One component per file; colocate small helpers in the same file only if <15 lines
- Use `cn()` from `lib/utils` to merge Tailwind classes conditionally (clsx + tailwind-merge)
- Event handlers named `handle{Action}` inside component, `on{Action}` in props

## State & Data

- Server data: use RTK Query hooks (`useGetClientsQuery`, etc.) — never raw fetch or Axios
- Global client state: `useAppSelector` / `useAppDispatch` from `store/hooks.ts`
- Local UI state: `useState` for form inputs, tooltips, ephemeral UI
- Prefer derived/computed values over `useEffect` syncing
- Never call hooks conditionally

## Loading & Error States

Every component using RTK Query must handle all states:

```tsx
const { data: clients, isLoading, error, refetch } = useGetClientsQuery({ office });

if (isLoading) return <Skeleton className="h-40" />;
if (error) return <ErrorMessage message="Failed to load clients" onRetry={refetch} />;
if (!clients?.length) return <EmptyState title="No clients yet" />;
return <ClientList clients={clients} />;
```

## File Naming

- Components: `PascalCase.tsx` (e.g., `ClientCard.tsx`)
- Pages: `PascalCase.tsx` in `pages/` (e.g., `ClientDetail.tsx`)
- API slices: `camelCase.ts` (e.g., `clientApi.ts` in `store/api/`)
- Redux slices: `camelCase.ts` (e.g., `authSlice.ts` in `store/slices/`)
- Schemas: `camelCase.ts` (e.g., `client.ts` in `lib/schemas/`)
- Utils: `camelCase.ts` (e.g., `formatDate.ts`)
